rows.original:
Hmm. Tonight, what you most feel like is a quiet, restful night in — but there's restful and there's <i>restful</i>, so to speak. You climb onto your bed and nestle yourself up against the headboard, curl your legs sideways, then pat your thighs. Time for Ryn to get comf[silly
    |
    |y
].

"Those really do look like l[etheryn.lowConfidence
    |-l
]ovely pillows," she murmurs. "[etheryn.highConfidence
    |I don't mind if I do.
    |If that's where you think my head belongs, [pc.name]...
]"

It doesn't take long for your sweet elven lover to follow you and rest her head on your [pc.thighs]. Although the ice-blonde hair cascading loosely from her head provides a little bit of a buffer between your [pc.skinFurScales] and her algid skin, the coolness still seeps in... and it feels lovely. There's no danger of overheating with a chilly cutie like Ryn in your bed beside you — at least, physically. No guarantees when it comes to emotions, though.

She's enjoying herself, too. The cares of the day slowly disappear from Ryn's face as she rests quietly with you. Instead of fidgeting, she's the perfect picture of serene stillness; she lets you play with her hair, cradle her head, rub her long elven ears with nary a reaction save the growth of a calm, beatific smile. [etheryn.highConfidence
    |Terrified and shy she may no longer be, but something else still takes a visible toll on Ryn by the end of every day: her acute sense of[flags.WC_CLEAR
        | royal
    ] responsibility, which leads her to shoulder quite a heavy burden. Fortunately, you've got plenty of ways, big and small, to make that burden feel a little lighter. You're not sure whether you'd say that this is one of the big ways or the small ways, but judging from the placid elf in your lap, you know that it helps all the same.
    |It's not often that Ryn can just sit there and relax in someone else's embrace but you, for one, are determined to give her as many opportunities to do so as you can. To see the fearful, oft-abused princess be able to unwind and relax warms your heart. And to know that it's happening <i>because</i> you're there for her is almost more than you can bear.
]

Now's not the time to revisit the concerns of daytime. Instead, what time you don't pass in companionable silence is spent on relatively tranquil things. Ryn's got a bit of a musical bent, and sometimes [etheryn.lowConfidence
    |you encourage her
    |she chooses
] to hum [rand
    |upbeat marketplace music
    |romantic ballads
    |Lumian hymns
]; it's all frost-elven stuff, [flags.WC_CLEAR
    |[flags.RYN_DATE
        |quite
        |dimly
    ] familiar from your time in the Winter City
    |[pc.bg minstrel courtesan
        |easy enough for a pro like you to pick up
        |simple enough for even a foreigner like you to follow
    ]
], and by humming along with her you feel that much closer.

When a song is over and you turn back to talking, you keep your conversation on easy subjects, bedtime talk: fun things, rather than the stuff of nightmares. As Ryn rests on your thighs, she shares some of the good stories of her youth, few and far between as they must have been, and tells the legends and yarns of her people. And you reciprocate with your own home-brewed stories, with tales of your adventures before reaching[pc.bg barbarian hunter arcanist
    | this part of
] the Frost Marches, and with the kind of idle everyday [silly
    |meming
    |chatter
] that means little on its own but which serves as the conversational equivalent of comfort food.[etheryn.numKids 1
    |

    Inevitably, though, your and Ryn's talk eventually drifts to your [etheryn.numKids 2
        |children
        |kid
    ]: your excitement, your longing to be with them rather than adventuring, the little faces that they made the last time you saw them. It breaks both your hearts to have to spend any time at all away from them, even if they're far too young to ever remember your absence, and even though there'll be many long years together with them in the future. But there's a world that needs [pc.isDK
        |conquering
        |saving
    ]. <i>Their</i> world, now, as much as yours.
]

Yawns interrupt your repose a few times, but when they start to come more frequently, Ryn reluctantly abandons her thigh pillow for the real one. Under the blankets, side by side [etheryn.highConfidence
    |in each other's arms
    |with her in your arms
], the two of you are quick to fall into the untroubled sleep that you deserve.

